id #edb/ref 17592186514147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514147} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5cf5f8-e409-5012-a1e4-61c220034dce" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1122c444-72cf-52f8-8f20-6ea8a5da7c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513575} {:answer/id #uuid "209f4090-3596-58e7-8990-3c75de438426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513620} {:answer/id #uuid "5d06dde3-0cc6-5fef-aa3c-fb368c5d1065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513781} {:answer/id #uuid "74e49c08-fa40-5af5-8b36-283e9d1a618b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513840} {:answer/id #uuid "78c80181-9abd-5de7-a0e0-78fb4823c14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513840} :answer-field/id #uuid "76ffae76-26cc-5fc1-83ca-c7cd4df10103" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03af79c8-ec1b-5c46-ad78-8952f1107922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "spiral source" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513539} {:answer/id #uuid "83757963-4685-54bb-9868-c1c6c42c85bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "saddle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513875} {:answer/id #uuid "8d128a14-bf55-5328-82cb-18b8095cebe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "spiral sink" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513897} {:answer/id #uuid "9868e6ed-cdb9-57e4-89b1-02dc2eb6211d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513928} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74ac2ca-c624-58dd-9d66-708a048e2455" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31cd18d3-31d7-55f7-ad10-c12433b70f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513664} {:answer/id #uuid "33eb5ce8-21cb-5dab-887f-5d2b28165299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513672} {:answer/id #uuid "3952dbd1-9d2b-5554-ace1-337b0cc16846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513681} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca3d762-ccc2-5805-9e6a-7bc97a7df3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513689} {:answer/id #uuid "458ad91d-0bb7-57a4-8b00-34a42bfe3ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513718}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513672} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b73c3c-e37c-5ccd-b7bc-8a667a8d5029" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ec6a2eb-63e4-55a4-849b-ba0f89289e7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335018" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-0.5x+0.5xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=y-5xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0.2,\\,1]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is\n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=-0.5x+0.5xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=y-5xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-0.5x+0.5xy)=-0.5+0.5y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-0.5x+0.5xy)=0.5x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-5xy)=-5y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-5xy)=1-5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5+0.5y & 0.5x \\\\ -5y & 1-5x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5+0.5(1) & 0.5(0.2) \\\\ -5(1) & 1-5(0.2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.1 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0.1 \\\\ -5 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-(-5)\\cdot 0.1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+0.5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=\\pm 0.5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.$ Since the eigenvalues are purely imaginary, our equilibrium is $\\text{a stable}$ $\\text{center}.$\n\n**Note:**\nFor the Lotka-Volterra model (as in this problem), it is safe to classify the nonzero equilibrium as a center when the linearization has purely imaginary eigenvalues. \n\n**Watch out!** \nIn contrast, for a general nonlinear system, the Jacobian test alone is inconclusive (additional analysis is required to determine whether the equilibrium is a true center or a spiral sink/source)."} :step/id #uuid "a38583d0-39a0-55f8-a293-360a29886e88"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514532 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d905c7de-54bb-580c-ac14-3568c1b81457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370188}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370188} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0bd7840-6559-5707-b910-f2fb5c72d1d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69850b23-e61d-5814-b226-9ba564c143f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370190} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c7dbd36-88be-5be0-b944-7943dca6b4c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "340e7604-73de-5dd2-91e0-923f082f78e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-334999" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-2x+3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=7y-5xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Find the nonzero equilibrium of the model.\n\n$(${{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3xy=0 \\\\ 7y-5xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3xy & =0 \\\\ x(-2+3y) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=0$ or $y=\\frac{2}{3}.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $x=0,$ substituting it into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-5(0)y=0\\,⇒\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, one equilibrium is $(0,0).$\n\n- If $y=\\frac{2}{3},$ substituting it into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-5xy & =0 \\\\ y(7-5x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}(7-5x) & =0 \\\\ 7-5x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(\\frac{7}{5},\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero equilibrium of the model is\n$(\\frac{7}{5},\\frac{2}{3}).$"} :step/id #uuid "cc9846dd-5c6b-5fee-8018-43e9e9a516aa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514520}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514533 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6bc298-819c-5e72-8a93-83f08ec194c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396463} {:answer/id #uuid "8c621ff2-0784-5f4a-9f17-554f017a4290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "increases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396464} :answer-field/id #uuid "a630ba98-1096-5e16-a8ba-c72404307d8b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6ca0294-aea3-59be-887c-efcec2803859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "circles around" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396466} {:answer/id #uuid "b05325f4-1482-56b6-8efe-ae71cef71608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "approaches" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396466} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3c7d81-1bee-5ec7-956c-8dc539d9a494" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6db0a17e-67bc-5337-9db7-aa8831e48825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "decreases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396469} {:answer/id #uuid "285c3558-f151-51cd-8f5f-b1b41cc764e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "increases" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396470}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396469} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6eebb0b-3bd1-5fdc-aab2-c16f8bfe569f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff91e14-b9a5-586b-b8da-fd89429ce569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the nonzero equilibrium" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396472} {:answer/id #uuid "d16001f2-8334-5a4d-a5d3-2705ca6416c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the point of inflection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396473} {:answer/id #uuid "a5776bca-8e30-5c52-81a1-7c0faeb65e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396474}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396472} :answer-field/id #uuid "af8b3b57-c322-5cc0-b2e2-876f370e51d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc687ab5-118b-5439-986b-20786139182f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334754" :question/problem "![](images/71/718df02f2d0c2f01cc4a02a40da120178afe0f436bbf38cd5a8d249d87b5d1c9.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait above showing a solution of a Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-6y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x=x(t),y=y(t),$ and $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are positive constants.\n\nSelect the options below that best describe the dynamics of the system from point $A$ to point $B$ on the solution.\n\n$\\,$\nThe trajectory \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$\nThe number of prey {{field-3}} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{increases}.$"} :step/id #uuid "ce9debe6-891d-529c-892a-2636a0bb6427" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514532}}] :activity/title "The Lotka-Volterra Predator-Prey Model" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513513}]}
